  "notes": "Historical catalog year, built by fetching the real archived 2022-2023 bulletin edition directly (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2022-2023/undergraduate/colleges/health-human-development/kinesiology-bs/) -- and this one is genuinely different from 2023-2026, not a copy. Confirmed via direct fetch of both its 'Suggested Academic Plan' and 'Program Requirements' tabs: the 2022-23 Movement Science Option is listed at (56-58 credits) versus 2023-26's (40-42 credits) for the exact same 120-credit-minimum overall degree, because two real requirements were heavier that year: (1) PHYS 251 (Introductory Physics II, 4cr, real prereq PHYS 250/PHYS 211) was REQUIRED in addition to PHYS 250 -- 2023 onward dropped it, keeping only PHYS 250. Added PHYS 251 to Semester 6 here, right after PHYS 250's Semester-5 slot, matching its real archived 'Year 3 Spring' position. (2) KINES 495B (Field and/or Research Practicum) was a 6-credit requirement in 2022-23 (the archived Program Requirements table reads 'KINES 495B Field and/or Research Practicum in Kinesiology 6'), not the 3-credit version every later edition (2023-2026) uses -- updated the credits field on the existing KINES 495B item accordingly. To compensate for those +7 real credits and keep the overall total in the bulletin's own stated 120-credit range (rather than silently inflating the plan by 7cr), removed 3 of the template's 5 generic 'Elective (graduate school prerequisite)' slots (Semester 6's 4cr one, Semester 7's 3cr one, Semester 8's 3cr one = 10cr freed), keeping only Semester 5's two 3cr ones -- this matches the archived page's own real, much smaller generic-pool sizing for that year: its Program Requirements summary lists just 'Electives 0-2' for 2022-23 (versus 'Electives 0-16' every later edition), and its Suggested Academic Plan only has two ungrouped elective-type slots that year (both explicitly labeled 'Supporting Course (Possible Graduate School Prerequisite)', Year 3 Fall and Spring, 3cr each) rather than the four-to-five 'Elective (Suggest Graduate School Prerequisite)' slots spread across Years 3-4 that 2023 onward uses. Also confirmed the archived 2022-23 edition's own explicit, enumerated 'Select an additional 12 credits from approved 400-level KINES courses' list (rather than a generic 'except KINES 403' exclusion clause, which first appears in the 2023-24 edition) already omits KINES 403 by construction -- so the same 'match' regex this app already uses for every other year (excluding only KINES 403) is real and correct for 2022 too, not an anachronism. Also confirmed (same as every other year) that the archived 'Common Requirements for the Major (All Options)' list explicitly includes KINES 321 (3cr, prereq KINES 100) -- added to Semester 4 here for the same reason documented in KINES-2023.json's own notes (present in the real bulletin every year checked, including the current live 2026-27 edition's own Suggested Academic Plan table, but missing from the existing KINES-2026.json file's semester list). Everything else (MATH 26/140/22 pathway, CHEM 106/110 sequence, CAS 100A/B/C, STAT 200/250/SCM 200, the generic Elective-pool course list itself, the MATH 3/4/21/22 remedial chain for CHEM 110/106's real MATH 22 prereq, and max_credits_per_semester=18) mirrors the 2026 file's own modeling unchanged -- confirmed identical by direct fetch of the archived Movement Science Option's Additional Courses text.",
